{la broda be ko'a be'o noi brode} is "the one named "broda be ko'a be'o noi
brode"". {lo broda be ko'a ku noi brode} is "the one named "broda be ko'a"
which incidentally brodes". Relative clauses attached to the relativized
sumti themselves are still part of the name: {la broda be ko'a noi brode}
is "the one named "broda be ko'a noi brode"", and does not assert that
{ko'a brode}.

Does that answer your question? I'm not 100% sure I understand the original
question.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

